+# HA, RTO & RPO Runbook — Aegis
+
+This runbook documents steps to validate HA and RTO/RPO for critical services (Webhook, Milvus, Approver, Prometheus).
+
+1) Objectives
+- RTO (restore time) targets: Webhook 5m; Milvus partial recover 30m; Approver 10m.
+- RPO (data loss) targets: Webhook audit logs ≤ 5m; Milvus backups hourly.
+
+2) Pre-requisites
+- Have backup operator for Milvus and snapshot target (S3).
+- Prometheus & Alertmanager configured and oncall contact listed.
+- k8s cluster multi-AZ or multi-region nodes available for failover testing.
+
+3) Drill: Milvus restore (automated)
+- Step A: Verify latest backup exists in s3://<bucket>/milvus/
+- Step B: Scale down Milvus statefulset: kubectl -n aegis-system scale sts milvus --replicas=0
+- Step C: Run restore operator job to restore latest snapshot to a test namespace (scripts/restore_milvus_test.sh)
+- Step D: Scale sts to original replicas, verify collections exist, run sample queries.
+- Target: complete within 30 minutes. Document deviations.
+
+4) Drill: Webhook failover test
+- Step A: Record current replicas: kubectl -n aegis-system get deploy model-provenance-webhook -o yaml
+- Step B: Simulate outage: kubectl -n aegis-system scale deploy model-provenance-webhook --replicas=0
+- Step C: Attempt a sample validated deployment (should fail if enforcement=deny). Validate fallback behavior.
+- Step D: Restore replicas and verify request processing resume.
+- Target: identify failure modes and update HPA / HorizontalPodAutoscaler settings.
+
+5) Observability & Alerting verification
+- Ensure alerts for high latency or error rate fire within alert windows and route to oncall via Alertmanager receivers.
+- Validate Escalation & runbook link embedded in Grafana panels.
+
+6) Post-mortem & Improvements
+- Record start/finish times, blockers, and remediation tasks into MCP/Jira.
+- Update runbooks with discovered manual steps or timing constraints.
+
